    </programme>
    <programme start="20260704020000 +0800" stop="20260704030000 +0800" channel="311">
      <title>Diamond River Hunters 第1季第1集 -The Setup</title>
      <desc>Entrepreneur and adventurer, Peter Jago, and his team are on a mission to search for alluvial diamonds and gemstones washed in the hidden river valleys of Lesotho.</desc>
    </programme>
    <programme start="20260704030000 +0800" stop="20260704033000 +0800" channel="311">
      <title>Andy and Ben Eat Australia 第3季第1集 -South Australia</title>
      <desc>In the first part of the episode, Andy explores sustainable kingfish farming in Spencer Gulf, South Australia, visiting Clean Seas sea farm and preparing fresh kingfish sashimi with the team. Moving to Kangaroo Island, he learns pickling techniques with Kate from Kangaroo Island Source, showcasing her products in a Carne Asada Taco. The episode continues with Andy exploring d&amp;apos;Arenberg&amp;apos;s multi-function building and &amp;apos;The Cube,&amp;apos; experiencing a Chef&amp;apos;s Table, and concludes at Wirra Wirra winery, where he cooks Yogurt Flatbread with Olive Oil and Dukka, enjoying it with the staff and their wines.</desc>
    </programme>
    <programme start="20260704033000 +0800" stop="20260704040000 +0800" channel="311">
      <title>Andy and Ben Eat Australia 第3季第2集 -Northern Territory</title>
      <desc>In Kakadu National Park, Andy joins Dewayne Webb foraging pandanus and cooking Seared Buffalo with Pandanus &amp;amp; Charred Herb Salsa over an open fire. He then heads to Darwin, assisting Zach Green at Elijah’s Kitchen, a food truck offering indigenous-inspired meals like Magpie Goose and Crocodile Laksa. Returning to Kakadu, Andy goes fishing with local Barramundi expert Rob Johnson and prepares Paperbark Leaf BBQ Barramundi with Sour Tamarind Sauce at Anbangbang Billabong, showcasing the region&amp;apos;s environment and produce.</desc>
    </programme>
    <programme start="20260704040000 +0800" stop="20260704050000 +0800" channel="311">
      <title>Trucking Hell 第2季第5集 -Highlight 5</title>
      <desc>In this episode a 40-ton lorry rammed full of scrap metal overturns and spills its steel load across a major A road during rush hour, and Lantern recovery op Steve Knight is called to the scene. 25 tonnes of metal must be removed from the lorry before it can be lifted and with a damaged 5th wheel, it’s a job that will push Steve and his team to the limit. At Crouch HQ there’s excitement in the air as the team give trucking superfan Chris and his disabled daughter, the ride of his life by taking him to his wedding in a big orange truck. Late at night, recovery op Snod is called to the side of the M69 to recover two crashed cars. With one on its side with the hand brake off, he must take care righting it to make sure it doesn’t roll into the passing traffic. It’s particularly tough job for Snod as his friend was killed on the same stretch of road whilst recovering a vehicle.</desc>
    </programme>
    <programme start="20260704050000 +0800" stop="20260704060000 +0800" channel="311">
      <title>Trucking Hell 第2季第6集 -Highlight 6</title>
      <desc>This week a heavy rescue like no other – as father and son Dave and Adam Crouch team up to save a lorry transporting a train from sinking into soft ground. Crouch Recovery Op Jim must rescue a lorry from a ditch after the driver attempted an ill-advised three-point turn. And while Rory moves an antique fire engine for the boss, Fluff must get rid of a lorry load of stinking cheese…</desc>
    </programme>
